{
  "requirement": "During coverage-data preparation, on a terminal enabled under\n{cite}`requirements.test-coverage.processes.progress.terminal`, Habeas MUST\ndisplay updating activity and identify the current preparation stage.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.test-coverage.processes.progress.preparation`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text.** On an enabled terminal (stderr is a tty and `TERM` is not `dumb`), Habeas MUST do two things during coverage-data preparation:\n1. Display updating activity.\n2. Identify the current preparation stage.\n\nThe terminal-enabling policy, clearing, and the non-tty or `TERM=dumb` case belong to the cited `requirements.test-coverage.processes.progress.terminal`. I did not reassess those here, except to confirm that the subject's tests apply to an enabled terminal.\n\n**Stage identification.** The implementation sets two preparation stages: \"Preparing coverage: recording inputs\" in `Progress::preparation`, and \"Preparing coverage: capturing maps\" via `progress.stage` in `runner.rs#fn[run]`.\n- Unit test `progress.rs#mod[tests]/fn[stage_and_conversion_counts_are_visible_then_cleared]` uses a recording terminal. It asserts that the initial stage text appears and that, after `stage(...)`, the new stage text appears.\n- The PTY test `tests/execution_coverage.rs#fn[coverage_progress_on_a_pty_preserves_reports_and_plain_output_policy]` runs the real binary on a real pty with `TERM=xterm`. It asserts that both \"Preparing coverage: recording inputs\" and \"Preparing coverage: capturing maps\" appear.\n- Together these cover the \"identify the current stage\" obligation for each stage, both in unit isolation and end to end.\n\n**Updating activity.** `progress.rs#mod[tests]/fn[preparation_activity_keeps_updating_without_a_stage_change]` creates a preparation progress with no stage change. It polls the recorded frames until at least two distinct frames contain \"Recording inputs\", and requires an elapsed-time marker in each. This verifies that the display updates by itself (a tick or spinner) rather than only on stage change. The PTY test adds the check that escape sequences are emitted, so the display updates in place.\n\n**Enabled versus disabled terminal.**\n- The PTY test runs both `xterm` and `dumb`. For `dumb` it asserts there is no preparation or conversion display and no escape sequences. For a piped stderr it asserts the same. So the \"terminal enabled\" condition is exercised on both sides.\n- `NO_COLOR` is set, and the test asserts that progress still appears with no color sequences.\n\n**Failure and empty paths.** The PTY test covers a failing test, a missing profile, and a preparation error from an unreadable input. In the preparation-error case it asserts that the \"recording inputs\" stage is cleared before the \"Coverage preparation failed\" diagnostic. Those clearing obligations belong to the `terminal` requirement, but the test exercises them for the preparation stage.\n\nAll three tests carry `{test}` references to the subject. I found no unmarked relevant tests and no gaps.",
